A1 L1: jawa/alloc_probe calibrate on the game's Mono gives every counter a measured verdict against a known allocation (GC.GetAllocatedBytesForCurrentThread PASS/BLIND/OFF, BLIND expected) and one counter (GC.GetAllocatedBytesForCurrentThread itself if it works, else GC.GetTotalMemory or Profiler.GetMonoUsedSizeLong) agrees with the known large, small and 1 MB allocations within 10%
A2 L2: a >= 2000-tick metered window on a colony map with our mods yields a bytes/tick table per system (every component tick and tick list, ours included), no hook fault
A3 L2: the same window catches at least one GC landing >= 100 ms and names its trigger: an explicit GC.Collect (with its caller) or an implicit collection: no GC.Collect-family call in its frame (with the heap size it fired at)
